summary:
  The REC button goes back to recording whatever address the player holds,
  so a station playing through the timeshift tap records 127.0.0.1 — a port
  with one seat, already taken — and hands back an empty file.

history:
  Traced 2026-09-03 on the home machine. The relay is armed for every
  Ogg/Opus/FLAC station, relayserve.py seats exactly one client (the
  player) and closes its listener, and the recorder asked
  app.playerSourceString() for the address to fetch. canRecordUrl let the
  loopback URL through because streamFormat() reads an extensionless path
  as "unknown", which is neither hls nor playlist. Pressing REC on a FLAC
  station curled the shut port with --retry 20 and the completion handler
  reported __REC_EMPTY__. The title poller had met the same wall and
  already carried the answer — _icyStreamTarget() maps the tap back to
  the station — the recorder just never asked. This mutant puts the old
  question back.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RecordingEngine.qml

find:
          var url = app.upstreamSourceString();

replace:
          var url = app.playerSourceString();

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml
  test_the_rec_button_records_the_station_not_the_timeshift_tap: the
  REC_URL staging write must carry the station's address and never the
  127.0.0.1 tap. Line-neutral.
